        "audienceVibe": "Analytical executives, product managers, or operations leaders who respect data but have started treating percentages as abstractions.",
        "bridgeIn": "Picture a conference room in Toledo, Ohio, on a Tuesday morning in November, where a four-point-two percent line item on a quarterly slide was about to cost a company one-point-four million dollars\u2014and nobody in the room could explain why.",
        "bridgeOut": "That number on the next slide isn't a rounding error. It's a wet curb at four in the morning, and someone's hands trying to keep a promise.",
